WEBVTT

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:32.574
"Ms. Anzu Hoshino."

00:00:32.657 --> 00:00:33.658
PRODUCT TYPE: VIDEO GAME

00:00:33.742 --> 00:00:36.077
Yes! It's here!

00:00:37.203 --> 00:00:40.707
<i>My whole reason for living
is right here in my hands!</i>

00:00:41.833 --> 00:00:43.043
TALK ABOUT POP IDOLS WITH GIRLS
PLAY VIDEO GAMES WITH BOYS

00:00:43.126 --> 00:00:46.796
<i>In elementary school,
I always played video games with the boys.</i>

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:48.256
PLAY VIDEO GAMES WITH BOYS

00:00:48.339 --> 00:00:49.549
<i>In middle school…</i>

00:00:49.632 --> 00:00:51.509
Want to go to karaoke with us?

00:00:51.593 --> 00:00:54.763
<i>Instead of flirting with boys,
I preferred battling last bosses!</i>

00:00:54.846 --> 00:00:56.264
KARAOKE WITH CLASSMATES
HURRY HOME

00:00:57.974 --> 00:00:59.893
You're going to eat all that?

00:00:59.976 --> 00:01:02.187
Won't you get fat and bad zits?

00:01:03.104 --> 00:01:05.815
<i>And chocolate means everything to me!</i>

00:01:05.899 --> 00:01:08.318
NOPE, DON'T EAT THEM
DON'T WORRY ABOUT IT, GOBBLE IT DOWN

00:01:09.152 --> 00:01:10.737
<i>I love you!</i>

00:01:10.820 --> 00:01:14.407
<i>And my dearest love is Momohiki!</i>

00:01:14.491 --> 00:01:15.825
CUDDLE MOMOHIKI
KISS MOMOHIKI

00:01:15.909 --> 00:01:19.829
<i>Romance played
absolutely no role in my life. But then…</i>

00:01:24.417 --> 00:01:26.836
<i>I somehow found myself with this </i>ikemen<i>…</i>

00:01:28.797 --> 00:01:29.839
<i>in </i>yuka-don<i> style.</i>

00:03:11.983 --> 00:03:13.151
WHY IS THERE SO MUCH LEGALESE IN MAGIC!?

00:03:13.234 --> 00:03:15.028
Weekends are for video games!

00:03:15.111 --> 00:03:16.279
I'm all set!

00:03:16.362 --> 00:03:20.199
Okay! Let's play till dawn!

00:03:20.950 --> 00:03:22.869
ROMANTIC THRILLER

00:03:27.206 --> 00:03:30.376
Huh? Did they change the opening scene?

00:03:31.628 --> 00:03:35.590
Well, anyway, it's time to press "start"!

00:03:39.177 --> 00:03:41.596
Are you all right?
You're not hurt, are you?

00:03:53.358 --> 00:03:55.318
Huh? What's with this corny old lame game?

00:03:56.527 --> 00:03:59.197
In fact, this isn't even the right game!

00:04:06.996 --> 00:04:08.873
A fanfare, please!

00:04:09.540 --> 00:04:12.377
You've been selected as
the first test subject!

00:04:12.460 --> 00:04:14.337
Congratulations!

00:04:15.338 --> 00:04:18.800
I'm Riri, a wizard that makes
wishes and dreams come true!

00:04:19.384 --> 00:04:21.344
What? A wizard?

00:04:21.427 --> 00:04:26.599
It's very difficult to explain,
so please read this carefully!

00:04:28.101 --> 00:04:30.561
If this is a fantasy,
why so many Chinese characters?

00:04:30.645 --> 00:04:32.647
And the explanation is insanely long!

00:04:32.730 --> 00:04:35.066
You need to explain it
in just three lines!

00:04:35.149 --> 00:04:36.484
Like this?

00:04:36.567 --> 00:04:39.237
No! I mean make it simple to understand!

00:04:39.320 --> 00:04:41.281
Well, to put it simply,

00:04:41.364 --> 00:04:44.284
I've come all the way here
from the Magic World

00:04:44.367 --> 00:04:47.912
to help out people like you
who are total romance noobs.

00:04:47.996 --> 00:04:48.871
Keep your butt out.

00:04:48.955 --> 00:04:52.417
So when was the last time
you got a thrill from the opposite sex?

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:57.422
<i>Well, it was probably with
Lord Matthew or Swordsman Musashimaru.</i>

00:04:57.505 --> 00:04:59.507
Those are just characters in games.

00:05:00.008 --> 00:05:04.304
You're in high school now.
You need to dream bigger and get real.

00:05:04.387 --> 00:05:06.931
Didn't you say you make
wishes and dreams come true?!

00:05:07.015 --> 00:05:08.433
But…

00:05:08.516 --> 00:05:11.394
now that I'm here,
don't you worry one bit!

00:05:11.477 --> 00:05:15.648
<i>You've always ignored everything
that had to do with romance,</i>

00:05:15.732 --> 00:05:20.278
<i>so I've come to grant you
a life that's like an</i> otome <i>game!</i>

00:05:20.361 --> 00:05:24.407
Sorry, but everything you're saying
doesn't make any sense to me at all.

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:28.369
Well, you know
those romance games for girls?

00:05:29.203 --> 00:05:31.748
You're okay with them, right?

00:05:32.582 --> 00:05:33.416
I guess so.

00:05:34.125 --> 00:05:40.423
That's why I programmed this game
for you, our first test subject.

00:05:40.506 --> 00:05:43.634
Now you too can enjoy a life
that's like an <i>otome</i> game

00:05:43.718 --> 00:05:46.929
and be with a man like
the hero of <i>Romantic Thriller</i>!

00:05:47.013 --> 00:05:51.601
Did you watch the thrilling
and passionate opening video?

00:05:52.101 --> 00:05:56.647
I bet it was too much
for a total romance noob like you, Anzu.

00:05:56.731 --> 00:05:59.859
No, it wasn't!
The script and acting were so trite,

00:05:59.942 --> 00:06:01.778
it's clearly a lame game!

00:06:02.487 --> 00:06:06.574
For having zero romantic experience,
you act like an expert on virtual romance.

00:06:06.657 --> 00:06:10.244
You bet I do! Do you have any idea
how many <i>otome</i> games I've completed?

00:06:10.328 --> 00:06:13.873
<i>But when I tell you
that you'll be surrounded by </i>ikemen

00:06:13.956 --> 00:06:18.795
<i>like an </i>otome <i>game in real life,
you can't help getting a thrill, right?</i>

00:06:19.420 --> 00:06:21.255
What? In real life?

00:06:21.339 --> 00:06:22.298
That's right!

00:06:22.381 --> 00:06:23.716
In real life!

00:06:24.217 --> 00:06:26.135
Getting pressed against the wall…

00:06:26.219 --> 00:06:27.929
or getting your chin tweaked…

00:06:28.012 --> 00:06:32.391
or a kiss-filled real life
just might be waiting for you!

00:06:32.892 --> 00:06:35.520
-Seriously?
-Seriously!

00:06:36.062 --> 00:06:41.317
<i>And you'll be surrounded
by a dazzling array of </i>ikemen!

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:44.112
<i>My goodness, how busy you will be!</i>

00:06:44.612 --> 00:06:45.905
<i>Ikemen?</i>

00:06:45.988 --> 00:06:50.076
See? I'm starting to seem
more and more like an angel to you, right?

00:06:50.159 --> 00:06:53.579
But I've got my beloved Momohiki!

00:06:53.663 --> 00:06:55.373
Wait! Where's Momohiki?

00:06:55.456 --> 00:06:59.001
Momohiki! Hey! Where's Momohiki?

00:06:59.502 --> 00:07:02.713
To make sure
you focus entirely on romance,

00:07:02.797 --> 00:07:06.551
your three great desires in life,
video games, chocolate, and your cat,

00:07:06.634 --> 00:07:09.053
I have confiscated!

00:07:09.137 --> 00:07:10.638
What? Confiscated?

00:07:11.347 --> 00:07:13.933
You've got to be kidding.
There's no way you can do that.

00:07:16.352 --> 00:07:18.020
No way!

00:07:22.191 --> 00:07:23.234
See?

00:07:30.658 --> 00:07:33.119
All… All my game software

00:07:33.786 --> 00:07:37.457
has been turned
into "Kabayaki-chan Goro" eel jerky!

00:07:37.540 --> 00:07:40.209
Look! It's still "soft." See?

00:07:41.335 --> 00:07:42.211
What a lame joke!

00:07:42.795 --> 00:07:44.213
What about my chocolate?

00:07:46.799 --> 00:07:48.968
What? No way!

00:07:49.051 --> 00:07:50.970
The chocolate's all gone!

00:07:51.053 --> 00:07:53.848
The best part's been stripped off!

00:07:55.224 --> 00:07:56.559
Yes, it's been confiscated.

00:07:56.642 --> 00:08:00.480
Eating too much chocolate isn't good
for your skin and makes you flabby.

00:08:00.563 --> 00:08:02.648
What's that chocolate
on your mouth? Hypocrite!

00:08:03.232 --> 00:08:07.528
I guess you understand now what it means
to have your three desires confiscated.

00:08:07.612 --> 00:08:08.446
You bully!

00:08:08.529 --> 00:08:12.658
If you want something, you must
sacrifice something of equal value.

00:08:12.742 --> 00:08:17.497
Thinking you can have a hot-guy paradise
without any sacrifices is just absurd!

00:08:17.580 --> 00:08:18.748
You sadist!

00:08:18.831 --> 00:08:21.209
Be careful what you say.

00:08:21.292 --> 00:08:25.046
You see, I'm actually
quite a kind and caring wizard.

00:08:25.630 --> 00:08:28.382
I'm only doing this for your own sake.

00:08:28.466 --> 00:08:29.967
Are you trying to brainwash me?

00:08:30.051 --> 00:08:31.469
Is this some kind of cult?

00:08:31.552 --> 00:08:36.307
Unless I do this,
you'd choose that cat over any <i>ikemen.</i>

00:08:38.976 --> 00:08:40.353
<i>And when you're lonely,</i>

00:08:40.436 --> 00:08:43.689
<i>instead of seeing your boyfriend,
you'd comfort yourself with chocolate.</i>

00:08:44.732 --> 00:08:48.945
<i>And instead of spending time on dates,
you'd rather play video games.</i>

00:08:50.738 --> 00:08:52.406
Do you understand now

00:08:52.490 --> 00:08:56.410
just how much your three great desires
prevent you from having a romance?

00:08:56.494 --> 00:09:00.498
Until you have an actual thrilling romance
like in <i>Romantic Thriller</i>,

00:09:00.581 --> 00:09:04.085
these things will be forever confiscated!

00:09:04.168 --> 00:09:05.002
FOREVER CONFISCATED

00:09:05.086 --> 00:09:06.879
That would kill me!

00:09:07.922 --> 00:09:10.007
<i>I wouldn't last even a single day!</i>

00:09:11.008 --> 00:09:13.177
I can live without <i>ikemen!</i>

00:09:13.261 --> 00:09:17.682
But my three great desires
are essential for me to live!

00:09:17.765 --> 00:09:20.351
That's exactly why you were selected!

00:09:20.434 --> 00:09:21.602
Remember what I said?

00:09:21.686 --> 00:09:25.690
We've come here to solve
Japan's dwindling population problem.

00:09:26.357 --> 00:09:28.734
Dwindling population? You never said that!

00:09:28.818 --> 00:09:32.572
I knew it! You didn't properly read
the explanation at the very beginning.

00:09:34.323 --> 00:09:35.199
At any rate,

00:09:35.283 --> 00:09:39.453
I will do everything in my power
to help you find romance, Anzu.

00:09:39.537 --> 00:09:41.706
All for the sake of love,
for Japan's future,

00:09:41.789 --> 00:09:44.417
and most of all, for my salary!

00:09:44.500 --> 00:09:46.836
I didn't need to hear that last part!

00:09:46.919 --> 00:09:48.671
Oh, dear!

00:09:48.754 --> 00:09:51.632
I left a pot boiling on the stove!

00:09:51.716 --> 00:09:54.802
Anyway, I'd better be
getting back to the Magic World.

00:09:54.885 --> 00:09:57.013
I'm not going to be part of this!

00:09:57.096 --> 00:09:59.140
<i>But you pushed the start button earlier.</i>

00:09:59.223 --> 00:10:01.475
No can do.
You've already boarded this ship.

00:10:01.559 --> 00:10:03.978
You have to ride in it,
even if it's made of mud.

00:10:04.061 --> 00:10:05.396
I won't ride in any mud boat!

00:10:05.479 --> 00:10:07.898
I'm just kidding
about it being made of mud.

00:10:07.982 --> 00:10:11.777
Actually, it's a Titanic-sized love boat!

00:10:12.737 --> 00:10:14.905
But that thing sunk too!

00:10:14.989 --> 00:10:18.784
How can a life without
my three great desires be any good?

00:10:18.868 --> 00:10:21.162
Give me back my purpose in life!

00:10:21.245 --> 00:10:23.623
I'll be seeing you! Bon voyage!

00:10:23.706 --> 00:10:25.833
Hey! Darn you!

00:10:28.836 --> 00:10:30.546
Mom! Where's Momohiki?

00:10:30.630 --> 00:10:32.715
Up there.

00:10:32.798 --> 00:10:35.217
What's Momohiki doing up there?

00:10:35.301 --> 00:10:39.597
Momohiki! Show me your sweet face! Please!

00:10:40.181 --> 00:10:41.140
I'm home!

00:10:42.725 --> 00:10:43.643
Oh, my!

00:10:43.726 --> 00:10:45.478
You sure are home early today, honey.

00:10:45.561 --> 00:10:48.147
Yeah. Now, I know this is really sudden,

00:10:48.773 --> 00:10:51.442
but I've been transferred to the US.

00:10:51.525 --> 00:10:52.693
Oh, my goodness!

00:10:53.986 --> 00:10:55.738
And you'll come with me, dear.

00:10:55.821 --> 00:10:59.325
I've always wanted to live abroad!

00:11:00.242 --> 00:11:02.286
Wait! What about me?

00:11:02.370 --> 00:11:04.288
You've got school, Anzu.

00:11:04.372 --> 00:11:05.998
It's only a couple of years.

00:11:06.082 --> 00:11:08.834
You're old enough
to live on your own that long.

00:11:09.418 --> 00:11:11.462
Wait! Things are changing so fast!

00:11:12.421 --> 00:11:14.173
<i>Wait a minute here!</i>

00:11:14.256 --> 00:11:16.509
<i>I thought Dad worked for the post office.</i>

00:11:16.592 --> 00:11:18.344
<i>Why is he transferred to the US?</i>

00:11:19.929 --> 00:11:21.639
We need to start packing right away.

00:11:21.722 --> 00:11:23.724
I'll make us a special dinner tonight.

00:11:28.062 --> 00:11:29.480
Okay, we'll be going.

00:11:29.563 --> 00:11:32.900
Make sure you eat right.
And lock up properly when you go out.

00:11:33.484 --> 00:11:35.236
-See you later!
-See you later!

00:11:38.364 --> 00:11:41.826
How can they prep
so fast to move overseas?

00:11:41.909 --> 00:11:44.328
And never mind that they
are so incredibly flexible,

00:11:44.412 --> 00:11:48.416
how can they force their
high-school daughter to live alone?

00:11:49.250 --> 00:11:52.711
It's important to get things
ready for you as quickly as possible.

00:12:03.806 --> 00:12:07.017
Now that I'm overflowing with frustration,
I've got heaps of energy!

00:12:07.101 --> 00:12:08.561
Say your prayers!

00:12:08.644 --> 00:12:09.562
As I predicted,

00:12:09.645 --> 00:12:12.982
you're perfectly suited
to be the non-heroine.

00:12:13.065 --> 00:12:14.775
NON-HEROINE

00:12:15.818 --> 00:12:17.820
I'm happy being the non-heroine!

00:12:17.903 --> 00:12:19.822
Now switch things back
to the way they were!

00:12:19.905 --> 00:12:22.324
Give me back Momohiki!

00:12:22.408 --> 00:12:23.242
Impossible!

00:12:28.497 --> 00:12:30.291
Darn it all!

00:12:31.792 --> 00:12:32.751
You're kidding!

00:12:32.835 --> 00:12:34.753
-Chocolate!
-So sorry.

00:12:34.837 --> 00:12:36.755
-Chocolate!
-We're closed.

00:12:36.839 --> 00:12:39.383
-Chocolate!
-We're having a wheat gluten sweets sale!

00:12:39.467 --> 00:12:41.385
ON SALE
MANAGER'S CHOICE

00:12:42.052 --> 00:12:42.970
Seriously?

00:12:44.096 --> 00:12:46.932
Everything's sold out?
Is that even possible?

00:12:48.392 --> 00:12:53.939
Have I been cursed so I can never
taste chocolate again in my life?

00:12:54.899 --> 00:12:57.776
There's no more chocolate. No more cocoa.

00:12:58.527 --> 00:13:01.697
Why… Why has this happened to me?

00:13:01.780 --> 00:13:04.783
How can this be?

00:13:05.367 --> 00:13:08.496
<i>I couldn't stand to be
under the control of that jerk who made</i>

00:13:08.579 --> 00:13:10.539
<i>that lame</i> Romantic Thriller<i> game.</i>

00:13:14.126 --> 00:13:16.337
<i>I won't let that happen!</i>

00:13:16.420 --> 00:13:19.798
<i>If some </i>ikemen<i> shows up,
I just won't fall in love!</i>

00:13:20.341 --> 00:13:25.054
<i>No mere mortal man can possibly live up
to the impossibly high expectations</i>

00:13:25.137 --> 00:13:27.181
<i>I've built up by playing video games!</i>

00:13:28.474 --> 00:13:30.893
<i>If there's never any romance,</i>

00:13:30.976 --> 00:13:36.732
<i>then that loser creep is sure
to give up and leave me alone!</i>

00:13:39.568 --> 00:13:44.198
<i>Depriving me of my three great desires
has transformed me into a heinous beast!</i>

00:13:44.782 --> 00:13:48.202
<i>This won't be any
pathetic</i> Romantic Thriller<i>.</i>

00:13:48.285 --> 00:13:50.204
<i>I'll blow this whole thing to bits</i>

00:13:50.287 --> 00:13:54.375
and transform into a romantic killer!

00:13:59.338 --> 00:14:03.217
I'm ready now! Bring on the <i>ikemen!</i>

00:14:11.225 --> 00:14:12.685
I'm sorry!

00:14:15.646 --> 00:14:17.022
Dang, it's shattered.

00:14:18.566 --> 00:14:20.693
<i>It's an </i>ikemen<i> already!</i>

00:14:22.653 --> 00:14:24.780
I'm sorry! I'll pay for it!

00:14:25.281 --> 00:14:28.576
-You don't have to pay.
-What?

00:14:28.659 --> 00:14:31.495
I wasn't watching where I was going.

00:14:34.665 --> 00:14:38.961
<i>Compared to Matthew and Musashimaru,
he's no big deal at all!</i>

00:14:40.546 --> 00:14:43.549
In that case, thank you!

00:14:43.632 --> 00:14:46.760
Sorry about bumping into you. Bye!

00:14:57.730 --> 00:14:59.565
<i>See you later.</i>

00:15:02.860 --> 00:15:06.363
<i>What's the point in saying that
when nobody's even home?</i>

00:15:08.449 --> 00:15:12.202
<i>I totally can't believe how I bumped
into that </i>ikemen<i> yesterday.</i>

00:15:13.412 --> 00:15:17.750
<i>As long as I keep from getting
involved with them, it won't be a problem.</i>

00:15:18.417 --> 00:15:19.460
<i>Watch me, you sadist!</i>

00:15:19.543 --> 00:15:22.004
-Good morning!
-<i>Speak of the devil!</i>

00:15:22.588 --> 00:15:24.882
Okay! Let's head on into school together!

00:15:27.593 --> 00:15:28.469
What?

00:15:35.643 --> 00:15:37.853
Who said you could follow me?

00:15:37.937 --> 00:15:41.815
Don't you worry. Nobody else can see me.

00:15:41.899 --> 00:15:44.193
Maybe so, but you bother me!

00:15:44.276 --> 00:15:47.321
People will think I'm a nutcase
having conversations with myself.

00:15:47.404 --> 00:15:49.573
Don't worry about that either!

00:15:49.657 --> 00:15:54.578
While we're having conversations,
everyone else only sees an illusion.

00:15:54.662 --> 00:15:55.913
Nobody will ever know!

00:15:55.996 --> 00:15:58.874
You're still a pain
in the neck, so I'll ignore you.

00:15:58.958 --> 00:16:00.417
Well, guess what?!

00:16:10.511 --> 00:16:13.263
Don't underestimate
what I can do with my magic.

00:16:13.347 --> 00:16:15.975
That wasn't even magic just now!

00:16:16.058 --> 00:16:17.977
Before you retaliate, I'm out of here!

00:16:22.439 --> 00:16:25.025
<i>Isn't this the </i>ikemen<i> from yesterday?</i>

00:16:27.569 --> 00:16:28.862
<i>That school uniform…</i>

00:16:30.823 --> 00:16:32.741
<i>No way! We go to the same school?</i>

00:16:33.742 --> 00:16:34.910
<i>Darn that sadist!</i>

00:16:34.994 --> 00:16:36.120
You're not hurt, are you?

00:16:36.203 --> 00:16:40.290
I'm sorry. I'm such a klutz. Tee-hee-hee!

00:16:40.374 --> 00:16:42.835
<i>So this is what they were setting up!</i>

00:16:44.753 --> 00:16:46.755
Woah! Are you all right?

00:16:48.257 --> 00:16:51.010
Don't just stand there, Tsukasa.
Give her a hand.

00:16:52.386 --> 00:16:54.346
No! I'm perfectly fine!

00:16:54.430 --> 00:16:56.807
<i>No way in heck
I am letting that jerk get their way!</i>

00:17:03.897 --> 00:17:04.940
Bye then…

00:17:06.859 --> 00:17:09.194
Dang. He totally ignored me too.

00:17:16.452 --> 00:17:18.328
-There he is!
-Excuse me.

00:17:19.455 --> 00:17:21.040
I've always liked you.

00:17:23.042 --> 00:17:25.252
Will you please read my letter to you?

00:17:26.253 --> 00:17:29.673
<i>Woah! She's confessing her love!
The other girls think he's hot too.</i>

00:17:31.300 --> 00:17:32.426
That takes guts.

00:17:32.509 --> 00:17:33.510
No thanks.

00:17:35.012 --> 00:17:36.180
What?

00:17:38.849 --> 00:17:39.892
Sorry.

00:17:41.018 --> 00:17:41.977
That's brutal.

00:17:42.061 --> 00:17:43.562
Poor girl.

00:17:43.645 --> 00:17:44.938
<i>What's with that?</i>

00:17:45.022 --> 00:17:47.649
<i>He may be an </i>ikemen<i>, but what a jerk!</i>

00:17:47.733 --> 00:17:50.319
Tsukasa! Good morning!

00:17:50.402 --> 00:17:52.446
I totally saw that just now!

00:17:53.113 --> 00:17:54.782
But I know how you feel.

00:17:54.865 --> 00:17:57.534
A letter in this day and age is so passé.

00:17:57.618 --> 00:18:00.412
You think so? I'd totally love to get one!

00:18:00.496 --> 00:18:02.831
You could've at least accepted it.

00:18:05.125 --> 00:18:06.752
She'd just get the wrong idea.

00:18:08.087 --> 00:18:10.547
I totally know how you feel.
She's not even your type.

00:18:10.631 --> 00:18:11.507
<i>Dang!</i>

00:18:11.590 --> 00:18:14.259
<i>All his popularity has made him conceited!</i>

00:18:14.343 --> 00:18:16.887
<i>No way in heck
I'm ever dating a jerk like that!</i>

00:18:16.970 --> 00:18:20.599
By the way,
you didn't read any of my texts yesterday.

00:18:20.682 --> 00:18:21.975
My phone's busted.

00:18:26.772 --> 00:18:28.732
-Yikes!
-You got insurance?

00:18:28.816 --> 00:18:30.067
I'm too cheap to get one.

00:18:30.567 --> 00:18:31.944
That's so insane!

00:18:32.027 --> 00:18:34.446
I would just die
if I didn't have a cell phone!

00:18:34.530 --> 00:18:36.824
Aren't you going to buy a new one?

00:18:36.907 --> 00:18:39.243
Not for a while. I'm broke.

00:18:39.326 --> 00:18:40.285
Really?

00:18:44.331 --> 00:18:45.207
<i>For real?</i>

00:18:45.874 --> 00:18:48.210
Your dad got transferred overseas?

00:18:48.794 --> 00:18:49.711
Yeah.

00:18:49.795 --> 00:18:52.714
I didn't even have time
to make lunch this morning.

00:18:53.298 --> 00:18:55.467
Sorry to make you come with me, Saki.

00:18:55.551 --> 00:18:58.512
It's okay. I look forward
to my first time in the cafeteria.

00:18:58.595 --> 00:19:02.391
You're right.
Let me see. What should I get?

00:19:02.474 --> 00:19:04.518
What do you want?
I'll order for both of us.

00:19:04.601 --> 00:19:06.353
I know!

00:19:06.436 --> 00:19:07.771
Then I'll have…

00:19:08.355 --> 00:19:09.481
-The A lunch.
-The A lunch.

00:19:17.447 --> 00:19:22.161
Isn't that guy Kazuki, the hot stud
everyone talks about from class seven?

00:19:22.953 --> 00:19:24.288
Kazuki?

00:19:25.205 --> 00:19:26.290
Is that so?

00:19:27.249 --> 00:19:29.835
The girls are always talking about him.

00:19:29.918 --> 00:19:34.006
Since you're always playing video games
on lunch break, you don't know about him.

00:19:37.926 --> 00:19:40.637
I heard he moved here alone
from outside the prefecture.

00:19:41.638 --> 00:19:44.683
He's popular since he's so chill
and hardly ever smiles.

00:19:44.766 --> 00:19:46.059
Really?

00:19:46.143 --> 00:19:47.019
No thanks.

00:19:47.978 --> 00:19:50.272
She'd just get the wrong idea.

00:19:51.190 --> 00:19:52.983
<i>I guess you'd call that "chill."</i>

00:19:53.066 --> 00:19:55.944
<i>But it seems to me
that he's more like a jerk.</i>

00:19:56.028 --> 00:20:00.866
Hating him at first but gradually
falling in love is typically how it goes.

00:20:00.949 --> 00:20:01.783
Buzz off!

00:20:04.328 --> 00:20:06.496
-Time to chow down!
-Tsukasa!

00:20:06.580 --> 00:20:08.582
I'll take this seat next to you.

00:20:09.708 --> 00:20:12.961
You know, I heard
that you live alone, Tsukasa.

00:20:13.045 --> 00:20:15.839
That's so awesome!
Can I come over for a visit?

00:20:15.923 --> 00:20:17.633
Where do you live?

00:20:17.716 --> 00:20:20.469
<i>No! I can't hear this! I can't hear it!</i>

00:20:21.553 --> 00:20:24.723
<i>I've got to shut out
everything I don't want to know!</i>

00:20:24.806 --> 00:20:27.935
<i>From now on,
I'll avoid using the cafeteria all I can!</i>

00:20:32.731 --> 00:20:34.733
I've got nothing to do!

00:20:35.400 --> 00:20:36.276
I'm bored.

00:20:39.488 --> 00:20:42.741
What the heck do people do
if they can't play video games?

00:20:43.575 --> 00:20:45.661
No Momohiki either.

00:20:45.744 --> 00:20:47.079
No chocolate either.

00:20:53.877 --> 00:20:55.504
I'll make dinner.

00:21:06.807 --> 00:21:09.768
<i>Since it is unsightly,
we've converted it to a slice of cake.</i>

00:21:14.022 --> 00:21:14.856
THE GLASS IS IMAGINARY

00:21:14.940 --> 00:21:17.442
Mom!

00:21:22.406 --> 00:21:26.034
Oh, that's right!
The roach extermination expert is gone!

00:21:26.118 --> 00:21:28.036
She always handled them for us!

00:21:33.166 --> 00:21:37.087
<i>Arise! It's time
for the soldier in me to emerge!</i>

00:21:39.631 --> 00:21:41.091
Go!

00:21:44.219 --> 00:21:46.430
Dang thing's empty!

00:21:55.856 --> 00:21:58.191
Roach!

00:22:04.823 --> 00:22:07.784
I was in such a hurry,
I didn't bring anything with me.

00:22:07.868 --> 00:22:09.536
Even my sandals don't match.

00:22:10.329 --> 00:22:14.291
I don't want to go home, but I'm starving.

00:22:14.374 --> 00:22:16.335
Mommy!

00:22:21.631 --> 00:22:23.675
Could it get any worse?

00:22:23.759 --> 00:22:25.635
I've got to get out of this rain!

00:22:40.150 --> 00:22:42.360
It's not letting up at all.

00:23:05.008 --> 00:23:06.510
A fanfare, please!

00:23:06.593 --> 00:23:08.678
Congratulations!

00:23:08.762 --> 00:23:14.184
I bet you're so interested in
what comes next, you can't skip this bit!

00:23:14.267 --> 00:23:17.854
We live in a time where
we can choose what we want to watch.

00:23:17.938 --> 00:23:21.525
But what have we lost along the way?

00:23:21.608 --> 00:23:22.984
Don't say you don't want to change.

00:23:23.068 --> 00:23:25.654
Explore more
and live a happy, sparkling life!

00:23:25.737 --> 00:23:27.656
For my salary's sake, that is.

00:23:29.991 --> 00:23:30.826
<i>Ah, yeah!</i>

00:23:33.453 --> 00:23:34.287
<i>Let's go!</i>

00:23:36.706 --> 00:23:37.958
<i>Lo-love!</i>

00:23:40.043 --> 00:23:40.877
<i>Here we go!</i>

00:23:40.961 --> 00:23:44.172
<i>Sorry that I'm forcing you</i>

00:23:44.256 --> 00:23:47.467
<i>But I promise you'll enjoy
A wonderful future</i>

00:23:47.551 --> 00:23:54.141
<i>No, no to your three greatest needs
Video games, chocolates, and cats</i>

00:23:54.224 --> 00:23:56.977
I'll never give myself up to these <i>ikemen!</i>

00:23:57.060 --> 00:24:00.522
That's what you say now,
but I know you'll give in eventually!

00:24:00.605 --> 00:24:02.232
<i>You! (So!) You too! (So!)</i>

00:24:02.315 --> 00:24:03.984
<i>I know your heart is beating fast! (Show!)</i>

00:24:04.067 --> 00:24:06.611
<i>Fall in love, no one can stop love!</i>

00:24:06.695 --> 00:24:09.197
<i>Come on, don't you want to fall in love?</i>

00:24:09.281 --> 00:24:10.532
<i>Just admit it</i>

00:24:10.615 --> 00:24:12.534
<i>Don't you want to fall in love?</i>

00:24:12.617 --> 00:24:13.743
<i>Don't be so stubborn now</i>

00:24:13.827 --> 00:24:15.787
<i>Don't you want to fall in love?</i>

00:24:15.871 --> 00:24:20.041
<i>You can't stay away
From these </i>ikemen<i> forever</i>

00:24:20.125 --> 00:24:22.169
<i>Come on now!
Don't you want to fall in love?</i>

00:24:22.252 --> 00:24:23.712
<i>Just leave it to me</i>

00:24:23.795 --> 00:24:25.839
<i>Don't you want to fall in love?</i>

00:24:25.922 --> 00:24:27.007
<i>Go ahead and lose yourself</i>

00:24:27.090 --> 00:24:29.092
<i>Don't you want to fall in love?</i>

00:24:29.176 --> 00:24:33.972
<i>You can't stay away
From these </i>ikemen<i> forever</i>

00:24:34.055 --> 00:24:35.307
<i>Embrace me, hold me tight</i>

00:24:35.390 --> 00:24:37.017
<i>Release your wild side</i>

00:24:37.100 --> 00:24:38.643
<i>The sign of love only you can pick up on</i>

00:24:38.727 --> 00:24:41.605
<i>Let's go romantic!</i>

00:24:41.688 --> 00:24:46.693
Subtitle translation by: Megumi Hunter
